.TH SFWC-THEME-APPLY 1 "" "sfwc" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sfwc\-theme\-apply \- render the templates of an sfwc theme for waybar, fuzzel, foot, mako, ...
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sfwc\-theme\-apply
.RB [ \-\-theme
.IR NAME ]
.RB [ \-\-config\-dir
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-templates
.IR DIR ]...
.RB [ \-\-out
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-skip
.IR NAME ]...
.RB [ \-\-no\-signal ]
.RB [ \-\-quiet ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Every
.I FILE.in
in a template directory is rendered to
.I FILE
in the output directory (default $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/sfwc). In a template,
.B @section.key@
is replaced by the value of that key of the theme (colors.*, geometry.*, shadow.*, font.*,
theme.name); colors are written #rrggbb, or with a modifier:
.BR :hex ,
.BR :hexa ,
.BR :rgb ,
.BR :rgba .
.B @@
is a literal @. Unknown keys are errors that name the file and line. The compositor runs this
program on startup and on every reload; outputs are only rewritten when their content changes,
and waybar (SIGUSR2) and mako (makoctl reload) are told to reload then.
.PP
Template directories, first match wins: <theme dir>/<theme>/templates, <config dir>/templates,
~/.config/sfwc/templates, ~/.local/share/sfwc/templates, /usr/local/share/sfwc/templates,
/usr/share/sfwc/templates. SFWC_TEMPLATES=dir[:dir] overrides the list.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 if the theme or a template was bad (the other templates are still rendered),
2 for a usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sfwc (1),
.BR sfwc.conf (5)
